SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 GMT: Royal Institute of Philosophy Essay Prize 2026:
  Humans and AI
DESCRIPTION:Closes 31 Dec 2026 at 23:59 GMT.\n\nThe Royal Institute of Phil
 osophy's annual essay prize asks for an original philosophical essay on th
 e 2026 topic\, Humans and AI. Essays of up to 8\,000 words\, anonymised fo
 r review\, are submitted by email. No eligibility restrictions are stated.
  Note: the Cambridge Core prize page still shows the older 2024 call at a 
 different amount\; the institute's own announcement is current.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Royal Institute of Philosophy\nLocation: Remote submission by email
 . Open internationally.\nAward: GBP 1\,000 cash plus GBP 500 of Cambridge 
 University Press books\; the winning essay is published in the journal Phi
 losophy.\nDuration: One-off essay prize.\n\nMore: https://royalinstituteph
 ilosophy.org/news/humans-and-ai-our-2026-philosophy-essay-prize-topic/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://royalinstitutephilosophy.org/news/humans-and-ai-our-2026-philos
 ophy-essay-prize-topic/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
LOCATION:Remote submission by email. Open internationally.
END:VEVENT
